[h1]🌎 Random New World[/h1]

[b]Sail west and find a world nobody has seen before, not even you.[/b]

Random New World replaces the Americas with a New World made from scratch and leaves the Old World as Paradox made it. New continents, coasts, mountains, climate, rivers, seas, resources, provinces and native peoples, different every time. Every world is a map mod of its own with a short [b]world code[/b]: a friend with the same game version makes the very same world from it.

[quote][b]Do not enable this item in a playset.[/b] It only carries the generator. The worlds it makes appear in your mod list as mods of their own: enable one of those.[/quote]

[h2]✨ What is in a world[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Five world types:[/b] Supercontinent, Continents, Small continents, Archipelago or Scattered islands.
[*][b]A living map:[/b] relief, climate, rivers, forests, deserts and jungles from one model.
[*][b]Seas:[/b] named gulfs, straits and capes, ports on every coast, ocean lanes and currents that continue the game's own.
[*][b]Native peoples[/b] with cultures, religions, tribes, states and vassals of their own.
[*][b]Extraordinary peoples:[/b] now and then a great empire, a league of sea-trading republics, a highland confederation, a fractured realm or a sacred centre.
[*][b]Stories and formable countries[/b] that grow from the world itself, and colonial names from its regions.
[*][b]No spoilers:[/b] the New World stays terra incognita until you play, even in the mod list and at country selection.
[/list]

[h2]🚀 Quick start[/h2]
[olist]
[*]In EU5's [b]Mods[/b] window press [b]Open in folder[/b] on Random New World and double-click [b]Random New World Generator[/b].
[*]Choose a world type. Keep the random seed, type your own or paste a world code.
[*]Press [b]Generate[/b]. In two or three minutes the world is in your mod list, for example as "RNW: Small continents 7K3Q".
[*]Enable that world, one at a time, and start a new game. If EU5 needs a restart first, the generator tells you.
[/olist]

[h2]⚙️ Make it your own[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]World basics[/b] answer in a word, as in EU4's random New World: land, native peoples and states, how often [b]Extraordinary peoples[/b] rise, gold and silver.
[*][b]Customize[/b] opens every value, and every value offered still makes a playable world.
[*][b]Choose a continent...[/b] sketches six seeds to pick from. [b]New peoples[/b] and [b]New resources[/b] roll one part again and keep the land.
[*]An atlas of every world: countries, cultures, religions, resources and development.
[/list]

[h2]🛡️ Why a program?[/h2]
A mod is data: it can change who owns what, but it cannot raise land, mountains or rivers. So a small program reads your EU5 installation and saves the world as an ordinary mod. It does not touch the game, uses no network and no administrator rights, and its code is open, with checksums published for every release.

[h2]⚠️ Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]New campaigns only.[/b] Generate the world before the campaign starts.
[*][b]Restart after a campaign.[/b] EU5 crashes when a different world starts after a campaign in the same session. Right after starting EU5, no restart is needed.
[*][b]Game updates.[/b] After an EU5 patch the generator may need its own update first. A save needs its world: make it again from its code.
[*][b]Memory.[/b] About 7.5 GB free while a world is generated.
[/list]

[h2]❓ FAQ[/h2]
[b]Can I see the map before I play?[/b]
Yes: [b]Reveal this world[/b] in the generator, or [b]Show the New World before you play it[/b] for the mod list and country selection too.

[b]Can I play a native country?[/b]
Yes. While the New World is hidden its countries are greyed out at country selection; show it for that world to pick one. [Confirm in the release sitting.]

[b]Other mods?[/b]
A world replaces the map, so it clashes with other map mods and with mods that rewrite the Americas. [Until tested:] Others are untested.

[b]Multiplayer?[/b]
Every player makes the world from the same code with the same game version, and it comes out identical. [Until tested:] A multiplayer game is untested.

[b]Ironman and achievements?[/b]
Like other mods that change the game, a world changes the checksum. [Confirm what EU5 allows.]

[b]Do my worlds need the generator?[/b]
No. A world plays on its own and stays after you unsubscribe.

[b]Windows warns me.[/b]
Steam downloads are not marked as from the internet, so SmartScreen should not ask. [Confirm in 020.] Each release links a VirusTotal scan. [Until signed:] The generator is not signed yet, so Windows 11 Smart App Control stops it. [Once signed:] The generator is signed by [signer].

[b]Linux or Steam Deck?[/b]
[b]Open in folder[/b] opens Wine's file explorer, and the generator runs in the game's own Proton prefix. Nothing to install. [Steam Deck: confirm.]

[b]How do I remove it?[/b]
[b]Delete world[/b] in the generator, then unsubscribe.

[b]I found a bug.[/b]
Press [b]Save diagnostics[/b] in the generator's [b]Settings[/b] (your name and folders are blanked) and attach the file and the world code to a report on GitHub.

